# launcher/boot/kernel-cmdline — canonical kernel command line.
#
# This file documents the exact cmdline string that ends up measured
# into RTMR1 by the TDX virtual firmware.  It MUST stay in lock-step
# with mkosi/mkosi.conf KernelCommandLine — any drift means the image
# you ship and the image governance approved differ.
#
# The build pipeline (build/build.sh) sources this file, computes the
# canonical single-line cmdline, and rejects the build if it does not
# match mkosi.conf.
#
# Order matters because the kernel command line is hashed as a flat
# string into RTMR1; reordering produces a different measurement.

# === Behavior ===
quiet
selinux=0
audit=0
console=null
loglevel=3
systemd.show_status=false
rd.systemd.show_status=false
rd.udev.log_priority=3

# === Randomness ===
random.trust_cpu=on

# === Failure mode ===
oops=panic
panic=10

# === Memory hardening ===
slab_nomerge
page_alloc.shuffle=1
init_on_alloc=1
init_on_free=1
randomize_kstack_offset=on

# === Attack-surface reduction ===
vsyscall=none
debugfs=off
lockdown=confidentiality

# === Rootfs (filled in by build pipeline; see boot/dm-verity-build.sh) ===
# root=PARTUUID=...
# rd.systemd.verity=yes
# roothash=...
# systemd.verity_root_data=...
# systemd.verity_root_hash=...
